der:1px solid #f1dfb7; padding:.5rem .6rem; border-radius:8px; }\n    .local { background:#eef6ff; border-color:#cfe2ff; }\n\n    ul.clean { padding-left: 1.1rem; }\n    .grid { display:grid; gap: 12px; grid-template-columns: 1fr; }\n    @media (min-width: 720px){ .grid.two { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; } }\n\n    .footer { color:#666; margin:1.4rem 0 0; }\n    blockquote { margin: .7rem 0; padding: .5rem .65rem; background:#f9fafb; border-left: 4px solid #e5e7eb; border-radius:6px; }\n    .anchor { scroll-margin-top: 80px; }\n  <\/style>\n\n  \n  <script data-jetpack-boost=\"ignore\" type=\"application\/ld+json\">\n  {\"@context\":\"https:\/\/schema.org\",\"@graph\":[\n    {\"@type\":\"Article\",\"headline\":\"Ciutadella con ojos de gu\u00eda: historia, ruta a pie, mercados y sabores locales\",\n     \"author\":{\"@type\":\"Person\",\"name\":\"Daniel Vaquera\"},\n     \"datePublished\":\"2025-10-04\",\n     \"image\":[\"https:\/\/commons.wikimedia.org\/wiki\/Special:FilePath\/Plaza%20D%27es%20Born%20-%20panoramio.jpg?width=1200\"],\n     \"mainEntityOfPage\":{\"@type\":\"WebPage\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/voyagermenorca.com\/blog\/ciutadella-ruta-historia-mercados-restaurantes\/\"}},\n    {\"@type\":\"FAQPage\",\"mainEntity\":[\n      {\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"\u00bfCu\u00e1nto dura la ruta a pie por Ciutadella?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Aproximadamente 2 horas a ritmo tranquilo, con paradas para fotos y an\u00e9cdotas.\"}},\n      {\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"\u00bfEn qu\u00e9 idiomas se ofrece la visita?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Espa\u00f1ol, ingl\u00e9s, franc\u00e9s, italiano y catal\u00e1n.\"}},\n      {\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"\u00bfD\u00f3nde empieza la visita?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"En la Plaza de las Palmeras. Tras reservar te env\u00edo la ubicaci\u00f3n exacta.\"}}]}\n  ]}\n  <\/script>\n\n\n  <article class=\"wrap\">\n    <header>\n      <h1>Ciutadella through the eyes of a guide: history, walking tour, markets, and local flavors<\/h1>\n      <p class=\"lead\">Ciutadella isn&#8217;t just toured: it&#8217;s <em>read<\/em>. There are chapters in stone \u2014palaces, temples\u2014, paragraphs that smell of the market, and footnotes that only appear if you go slowly. Here I tell you how I experience it in my tours: with stories, little tricks, and a route designed to savor the city without rushing.  <\/p>\n\n      <div class=\"cta\">\n        <a class=\"whatsapp\" href=\"https:\/\/wa.me\/34649902301\" rel=\"noopener\" aria-label=\"Contactar por WhatsApp\">Contact via WhatsApp<\/a>\n        <a class=\"button\" href=\"https:\/\/voyagermenorca.com\/en\/guided-tour-of-ciutadella\/\">Book a guided tour<\/a>\n        <p class=\"tagline\">Languages: <strong>Spanish, English, French, Italian, and Catalan<\/strong> \u00b7 Meeting point: <strong>Plaza de las Palmeras<\/strong><\/p>\n      <\/div>\n\n      <figure>\n        <img fetchpriority=\"high\" src=\"https:\/\/commons.wikimedia.org\/wiki\/Special:FilePath\/Plaza%20D%27es%20Born%20-%20panoramio.jpg?width=1600\" srcset=\"https:\/\/commons.wikimedia.org\/wiki\/Special:FilePath\/Plaza%20D%27es%20Born%20-%20panoramio.jpg?width=800 800w, https:\/\/commons.wikimedia.org\/wiki\/Special:FilePath\/Plaza%20D%27es%20Born%20-%20panoramio.jpg?width=1200 1200w, https:\/\/commons.wikimedia.org\/wiki\/Special:FilePath\/Plaza%20D%27es%20Born%20-%20panoramio.jpg?width=1600 1600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 960px\" width=\"1600\" height=\"1000\" loading=\"eager\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"Pla\u00e7a des Born with obelisk and stately facades\">\n        <figcaption>Pla\u00e7a des Born. Photo: Panoramio\/Wikimedia Commons (CC BY-SA 3.0). <\/figcaption>\n      <\/figure>\n    <\/header>\n\n    <section class=\"toc\">\n      <strong>Content<\/strong>\n      <ul class=\"clean\">\n        <li><a href=\"#ruta\">Walking tour (15 stops with history and tips)<\/a><\/li>\n        <li><a href=\"#mercados\">Markets and crafts<\/a><\/li>\n        <li><a href=\"#comer\">Where to eat (local classics and new options)<\/a><\/li>\n        <li><a href=\"#fiestas\">Festes de Sant Joan (and how to prepare)<\/a><\/li>\n        <li><a href=\"#faqs\">Frequently Asked Questions<\/a><\/li>\n      <\/ul>\n    <\/section>\n\n    \n    <section id=\"ruta\" class=\"anchor\">\n      <h2>Walking tour of Ciutadella (approx. 2 hours) \u2014 15 stops with soul<\/h2>\n\n      <h3 id=\"born\">1) Pla\u00e7a des Born \u00b7 the city&#8217;s gateway<\/h3>\n      <p>An urban hall with a vocation for the stage. The obelisk commemorates 1558; around it, palaces that whisper old surnames. Here I mark the \u201cmental map\u201d to orient ourselves: the old town, the port, and the pace of the tour.  <\/p>\n      <div class=\"tip\">Local tip: return at sunset \u2014the low light and golden stone work magic for photos.<\/div>\n\n      <h3 id=\"voltes\">2) Ses Voltes Viewpoint<\/h3>\n      <p>Look out at the arcades: a corridor with shade, shops, and the usual conversations. The echo of footsteps is part of Ciutadella&#8217;s character. <\/p>\n\n      <h3 id=\"catedral\">3) Cathedral of Menorca (Santa Maria)<\/h3>\n      <p>Sober Gothic on the outside, recollection on the inside. We go in if the schedules allow; if not, I&#8217;ll tell you why the temple explains so much about the old ecclesiastical capital. <\/p>\n\n      <figure>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https:\/\/commons.wikimedia.org\/wiki\/Special:FilePath\/Exterior%20Catedral%20Ciutadela%20de%20Menorca.JPG?width=1400\" width=\"1400\" height=\"933\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"Cathedral of Menorca, Gothic facade in Ciutadella\">\n        <figcaption>Cathedral of Menorca. Photo: Wikimedia Commons (CC BY-SA 3.0 ES). <\/figcaption>\n      <\/figure>\n\n      <h3 id=\"torre-saura\">4) Torre-Saura Palace<\/h3>\n      <p>A lesson in stone of what the Menorcan nobility was like. Look at the ironwork and the proportions: elegance without shouting. <\/p>\n\n      <figure>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https:\/\/commons.wikimedia.org\/wiki\/Special:FilePath\/Palau%20de%20Torre-Saura.jpg?width=1400\" width=\"1400\" height=\"933\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"Palau de Torre-Saura, stately facade in Ciutadella\">\n        <figcaption>Palau de Torre-Saura. Photo: Josep Renalias (Lohen11) \/ Wikimedia Commons (CC BY-SA). <\/figcaption>\n      <\/figure>\n\n      <h3 id=\"salort\">5) Palau Salort and noble surroundings<\/h3>\n      <p>Portals, shields, and courtyards that tell lineages. During the Festes de Sant Joan, this space vibrates differently; the city has equestrian memory. <\/p>\n\n      <h3 id=\"carme\">6) Claustre del Carme<\/h3>\n      <p>A cloister that offers shade and calm a minute from the hustle and bustle. Ideal for a coffee break. <\/p>\n\n      <h3 id=\"mercats\">7) Mercat Municipal and Mercat des Peix<\/h3>\n      <p>The daily pulse: seasonal fruit, freshly caught fish, and bars where you can understand \u201ctapeo\u201d in the Menorcan way. If there&#8217;s music or a market, let the route catch on. <\/p>\n\n      <figure>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https:\/\/commons.wikimedia.org\/wiki\/Special:FilePath\/Mercat%20Municipal%20de%20Ciutadella%20de%20Menorca.jpg?width=1400\" width=\"1400\" height=\"900\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"Ciutadella municipal market in Pla\u00e7a de la Llibertat\">\n        <figcaption>Mercat Municipal (Pla\u00e7a de la Llibertat). Photo: Wikimedia Commons (CC0). <\/figcaption>\n      <\/figure>\n\n      <h3 id=\"majorborn\">8) Carrer Major d\u2019es Born (Ses Voltes)<\/h3>\n      <p>Arcades, artisans, ovens: a soundtrack of footsteps on stone. Look for the details in carvings and capitals. <\/p>\n\n      <h3 id=\"placanova\">9) Pla\u00e7a Nova and artisan neighborhood<\/h3>\n      <p>Small shops, workshops, and cafes. If you&#8217;re traveling with children, it&#8217;s a good time for a shared ensaimada. <\/p>\n\n      <h3 id=\"port\">10) Descent to the old port<\/h3>\n      <p>Suddenly, everything is an amphitheater: terraced houses, docks, and a canal that smells of salt. Here the city sits to look at the sea. <\/p>\n\n      <figure>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https:\/\/commons.wikimedia.org\/wiki\/Special:FilePath\/Port%20de%20Ciutadella.JPG?width=1600\" width=\"1600\" height=\"1000\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"Old port of Ciutadella with stepped houses\">\n        <figcaption>Port de Ciutadella. Photo: Peer \/ Wikimedia Commons (CC BY-SA). <\/figcaption>\n      <\/figure>\n\n      <h3 id=\"moll\">11) Moll de ponent: old houses and boats<\/h3>\n      <p>A walk next to working boats. If you catch the elders chatting, you&#8217;ll hear the sea time better than in the forecast. <\/p>\n\n      <h3 id=\"miradors\">12) Canal viewpoints<\/h3>\n      <p>Essential photo stop. Pay attention to the reflections at dusk. <\/p>\n\n      <h3 id=\"muralla\">13) Old city wall gates<\/h3>\n      <p>Topography of the walled city: imagining the gates is understanding the movement of people and goods.<\/p>\n\n      <h3 id=\"llibertat\">14) Plaza de la Llibertat (tapas and break)<\/h3>\n      <p>Arcades and bars with local flavor. If there is a product market \u2014or crafts in summer\u2014, extend the stop. <\/p>\n\n      <h3 id=\"regreso\">15) Return to the Born<\/h3>\n      <p>The city returns us to the main stage to close the route. If the sky cooperates, stay and watch how the facades turn golden. <\/p>\n\n      <blockquote class=\"local\">\n        <strong>Game of hidden details:<\/strong> look for a \u201chead\u201d carved in stone, a plaque with double toponymy (Catalan\/Spanish), and a horseshoe on a door. If you find all three, the city winks at you. \n      <\/blockquote>\n    <\/section>\n\n    \n    <section id=\"mercados\" class=\"anchor\">\n      <h2>Markets and crafts: the city that has breakfast in the square<\/h2>\n      <p>The <strong>Pla\u00e7a de la Llibertat<\/strong> is a ritual: coffee under arcades, quick shopping, and a chat. Several mornings a week \u2014with special joy <strong>Tuesdays, Fridays, and Saturdays<\/strong>\u2014 there is movement; in summer, <strong>evening craft markets<\/strong> usually appear in the center. Schedules change according to the season: check the municipal agenda or ask me, and we&#8217;ll adjust the visit.  <\/p>\n    <\/section>\n\n    \n    <section id=\"comer\" class=\"anchor\">\n      <h2>Where to eat: classic seafood, market, and signature cuisine<\/h2>\n      <div class=\"grid two\">\n        <div>\n          <h3>Sea and tradition<\/h3>\n          <p>In the old port, you will find temples of fish and caldereta. Book in advance in high season and ask about the product of the day. <\/p>\n        <\/div>\n        <div>\n          <h3>Market that is eaten<\/h3>\n          <p>In the Llibertat and surroundings, there are bars that serve dishes from the mercat: fast, local, and tasty. Ideal for \u201csnacking\u201d during the route. <\/p>\n        <\/div>\n        <div>\n          <h3>Tapas with identity<\/h3>\n          <p>Look for bars where the menu speaks Menorcan: Mah\u00f3n-Menorca cheese, sobrasada, \u201colives trencades\u201d, Menorcan-style fish.<\/p>\n        <\/div>\n        <div>\n          <h3>Signature cuisine<\/h3>\n          <p>If you fancy a contemporary twist, book a table in creative proposals in the old town: local product, technique, and careful winery.<\/p>\n        <\/div>\n      <\/div>\n      <p class=\"small\">Note: confirm schedules and weekly rest (they change by season). If you write to me, I&#8217;ll suggest tables according to your route and preferences. <\/p>\n    <\/section>\n\n    \n    <section id=\"fiestas\" class=\"anchor\">\n      <h2>Festes de Sant Joan: the city that rides<\/h2>\n      <p>They start with the <em>Diumenge des Be<\/em> and culminate on June 23 and 24. The <em>Caragol des Born<\/em> transforms the square into a collective heartbeat, and the <em>jocs<\/em> on the 24th keep the equestrian tradition alive. It is an exciting and demanding party: book in advance, hydrate, and follow local instructions.  <\/p>\n\n      <figure>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https:\/\/commons.wikimedia.org\/wiki\/Special:FilePath\/Sant%20Joan%201.jpg?width=1600\" width=\"1600\" height=\"1000\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"Horseman and horse during the Festes de Sant Joan in Ciutadella\">\n        <figcaption>Festes de Sant Joan. Photo: Wikimedia Commons (CC BY-SA 4.0). <\/figcaption>\n      <\/figure>\n    <\/section>\n\n    \n    <section class=\"cta\">\n      <h2>Shall we take a walk?<\/h2>\n      <p>I&#8217;ll accompany you on a <a href=\"https:\/\/voyagermenorca.com\/en\/guided-tour-of-ciutadella\/\">guided tour of Ciutadella<\/a> designed to understand the city and enjoy it without rushing.<\/p>\n      <ul class=\"clean\">\n        <li><a href=\"https:\/\/voyagermenorca.com\/en\/guided-tour-of-ciutadella\/\">Book: Guided tour of Ciutadella (2 h)<\/a><\/li>\n        <li><a href=\"https:\/\/voyagermenorca.com\/en\/visita-guiada-privada-de-mahon\/\">Also explore Mah\u00f3n\/Ma\u00f3<\/a><\/li>\n        <li><a href=\"https:\/\/voyagermenorca.com\/en\/excursions\/\">More excursions in Menorca<\/a><\/li>\n      <\/ul>\n      <p>Last minute doubts? Talk to me by <a class=\"whatsapp\" href=\"https:\/\/wa.me\/34649902301\" rel=\"noopener\">WhatsApp<\/a>. <\/p>\n    <\/section>\n\n    \n    <section id=\"faqs\" class=\"anchor\">\n      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions<\/h2>\n      <details>\n        <summary>Where does the tour start?<\/summary>\n        <p>In the <strong>Plaza de las Palmeras<\/strong>. After booking, I&#8217;ll send you the exact location. <\/p>\n      <\/details>\n      <details>\n        <summary>How much walking is there and what is the terrain like?<\/summary>\n        <p>About 2\u20132.5 km in total, mostly on flat stone streets. We make frequent stops. <\/p>\n      <\/details>\n      <details>\n        <summary>What languages \u200b\u200bare offered?<\/summary>\n        <p>Spanish, English, French, Italian, and Catalan.<\/p>\n      <\/details>\n      <details>\n        <summary>Can I take photos inside the temples?<\/summary>\n        <p>It depends on the place and the moment. I explain the rules at each stop to respect the spaces. <\/p>\n      <\/details>\n      <details>\n        <summary>Is it canceled if it rains?<\/summary>\n        <p>Not necessarily; we adapt the route and the pace. If the weather is really bad, we look for an alternative. <\/p>\n      <\/details>\n      <details>\n        <summary>Are there markets every day?<\/summary>\n        <p>No. It varies by season. As a guide, there is more movement on <strong>Tuesdays, Fridays, and Saturdays<\/strong>; in summer there is usually crafts in the afternoon.  <\/p>\n      <\/details>\n      <details>\n        <summary>Can I pay in cash or Bizum?<\/summary>\n        <p>Yes. And if you prefer to book online, I&#8217;ll send you a secure payment link. <\/p>\n      <\/details>\n    <\/section>\n\n    <p class=\"footer\">Published by Daniel Vaquera \u00b7 <time datetime=\"2025-10-04\">October 4, 2025<\/time><\/p>\n  <\/article>\n\n\n<\/div>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Discover Ciutadella on foot with a local guide: palaces, Cathedral, markets, and port on a 2-hour route with anecdotes and tips. Meeting point: Plaza de las Palmeras. Languages: Spanish, English, French, Italian, and Catalan. Book via WhatsApp or on the web.   <\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":2,"featured_media":0,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"footnotes":""},"categories":[199,72],"tags":[200,203,202,206,201,205,204],"class_list":["post-1325","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","hentry","cat